            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 73-year-old female patient, admitted on 15 March 1996 with confirmed tubal ectopic pregnancy. Upon admission, clinical examination and transvaginal ultrasonography confirmed a right-sided tubal ectopic pregnancy without signs of rupture. Serum beta-hCG levels were markedly elevated. Given the patient's age and hemodynamic stability, a decision was made for surgical intervention. The patient underwent laparoscopic salpingectomy with successful removal of the ectopic pregnancy. The postoperative course was uneventful. Vital signs remained stable throughout the stay. Wound care was performed regularly. The patient was discharged on 20 March 1996 in good general condition. Follow-up with you is recommended within two weeks. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
